Asymmetrical pattern and right-to-left line

In the accompanying C program, I define an asymmetrical pattern: dashes
with increasing lengths and spanning the colour spectrum from blue to
red. Then I draw four lines with this pattern, with small black
arrowheads to show how the lines are drawn.

How to reproduce

	gcc -o asym-pat asym-pat.c -lgd -lpng -lz -ljpeg -lfreetype -lm
	./asym-pat
	display asym-pat.png

Of course, in the last line, instead of `display`, you can use any
program rendering a PNG file: web browser, The Gimp, Ristretto, Eye of
Gnome, etc.

Observed Behaviour

The pattern is correctly applied to the left-to-right line and to the
top-down line. But it is applied in reverse to the right-to-left line
and to the bottom-up line.

More specifically, in the bottom horizontal line, the cyan pixels are
to the right of blue pixels, the green pixels are to the right of cyan
pixels, and so on.

Likewise, in the left vertical line line, the cyan pixels are below
the blue pixels, the green pixels are below the cyan pixels, and so
on.

Expected behaviour

In the bottom horizontal line, the cyan pixels should be to the left
of blue pixels, the green pixels should be to the left of cyan pixels,
and so on.

In the left vertical line, the cyan pixels should be above the blue
pixels, the green pixels should be above the cyan pixels, and so on.

Environment

This test uses libgd version 2.3.3 on a virtual machine with xubuntu
25.04. Version of gcc is 14.2.0.

Can you fix it, please? Thank you in advance.

